            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/State/Reset.events.yaml",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "This can be really confusing to have two events. If really needed I would prefer just one which actually indicates a \"reset\". \n\nhttps://www.dmtf.org/sites/default/files/standards/documents/DSP2065_2025.3.pdf has PlatformReset but unfortunately, it just has one arg `string: The type of reset that occurred.` -- no mention of what.\n\n@paligill@gmail.com I noticed that all the Platform 1.3.1 message registry spec just assumes there is a \"computer system\" and does not really support multi-host systems or have the message registry provide the resource name/path etc."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/State/Reset.events.yaml",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "PeterYinGit",
                        "email": "peter.yin@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "PeterYinGit"
                    },
                    "message": "@amithash@meta.com @paligill@gmail.com\nIt seems that the schema in the Redfish specification is not suitable, so our plan is to only keep the ResetActivated, correct?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/State/Reset.events.yaml",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "ack"
                }
            ],
